1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,474
A customer calls Concrete again.

2
00:00:02,474 --> 00:00:07,577
What should the next customer service agent know before asking the first
question?

3
00:00:07,577 --> 00:00:09,383
Not just a phone number.

4
00:00:09,383 --> 00:00:11,474
but the correct customer profile

5
00:00:11,474 --> 00:00:12,974
the available history,

6
00:00:12,974 --> 00:00:15,916
and the notes attached to previous calls.

7
00:00:15,916 --> 00:00:20,022
Here's the second experience GRINDCTRL is proposing for Concrete.

8
00:00:20,022 --> 00:00:22,066
A clearer customer view.

9
00:00:22,066 --> 00:00:26,876
connected to incoming calls through Genesys and the appropriate Zoho
records.

10
00:00:26,876 --> 00:00:29,310
The caller number initiates a lookup.

11
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:31,213
After a reliable match,

12
00:00:31,213 --> 00:00:35,046
The agent sees the customer's name and permitted contact details.

13
00:00:35,046 --> 00:00:37,053
including email when available.

14
00:00:37,053 --> 00:00:39,900
Missing information is marked unavailable.

15
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:44,454
The same proposed view can show the customer segment from Concrete Icons
Club.

16
00:00:44,454 --> 00:00:45,429
Lifestyle.

17
00:00:45,429 --> 00:00:47,119
Prestige or Elite.

18
00:00:47,119 --> 00:00:51,773
That membership information must come from a trusted, updated source.

19
00:00:51,773 --> 00:00:54,196
It cannot be guessed from the caller's number.

20
00:00:54,196 --> 00:00:58,193
and no membership benefit should be assumed without confirmation.

21
00:00:58,193 --> 00:01:01,117
But a profile is only the starting point.

22
00:01:01,117 --> 00:01:03,466
Call level history matters more.

23
00:01:03,466 --> 00:01:07,660
Imagine a simple timeline showing every available call activity.

24
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:08,652
Its date?

25
00:01:08,652 --> 00:01:09,415
agent

26
00:01:09,415 --> 00:01:12,072
and notes for that specific interaction.

27
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:13,212
For example,

28
00:01:13,212 --> 00:01:16,217
Last week's call concerned an exchange request.

29
00:01:16,217 --> 00:01:19,398
The employee recorded that the branch would review the matter.

30
00:01:19,398 --> 00:01:21,518
When the customer calls again today,

31
00:01:21,518 --> 00:01:25,983
The new agent opens that particular call and reads its actual note.

32
00:01:25,983 --> 00:01:27,976
They see what was documented.

33
00:01:27,976 --> 00:01:30,925
Without confusing a call note with a ticket comment...

34
00:01:30,925 --> 00:01:32,034
AI summary,

35
00:01:32,034 --> 00:01:33,559
or a completed action.

36
00:01:33,559 --> 00:01:35,454
During today's conversation,

37
00:01:35,454 --> 00:01:39,752
The agent records a new note against the right interaction if supported.

38
00:01:39,752 --> 00:01:42,533
Notes should belong to the call they describe.

39
00:01:42,533 --> 00:01:44,323
not a generic summary.

40
00:01:44,323 --> 00:01:47,958
And the interface must handle uncertainty honestly.

41
00:01:47,958 --> 00:01:49,554
No matching contact?

42
00:01:49,554 --> 00:01:51,218
offer a manual search.

43
00:01:51,218 --> 00:01:52,674
Multiple matches?

44
00:01:52,674 --> 00:01:55,299
Ask the agent to select the right record.

45
00:01:55,299 --> 00:01:56,930
Missing membership data?

46
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:58,431
Mark it unavailable.

47
00:01:58,431 --> 00:02:00,212
Lookup temporarily down?

48
00:02:00,212 --> 00:02:02,325
Never block the incoming call.

49
00:02:02,325 --> 00:02:07,718
Before implementation, we'll verify where call activities and notes
actually live.

50
00:02:07,718 --> 00:02:09,547
which integrations are supported,

51
00:02:09,547 --> 00:02:11,984
and who is allowed to see each field.

52
00:02:11,984 --> 00:02:15,823
Then we'll test with authorized fictional customer records.

53
00:02:15,823 --> 00:02:18,686
The outcome we're aiming for is continuity.

54
00:02:18,686 --> 00:02:23,245
a more informed employee, and a customer who doesn't have to start from
zero.

55
00:02:23,245 --> 00:02:25,000
every single time.
